<title>USA: Lowe's Cos sells $100 million in notes.</title>
<headline>Lowe's Cos sells $100 million in notes.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following debt issue from Lowe's Cos was priced on Monday, according to lead manager Merrill Lynch &amp; Co Inc.</p>
<p>Lowe's Cos retails building materials, hardware, lumber, appliances via 394 stores in 24 states.</p>
<p>BORROWER LOWE'S COS</p>
<p>AMT $100 MLN	 COUPON 7.11 PCT   MATURITY 5/15/2037</p>
<p>TYPE NOTES	   ISS PRICE 100.00  FIRST PAY DATE 11/15/1997</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S A2    YIELD 7.11 PCT    PAY FREQ  SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P SINGLE-A  SPREAD +45/10 YR  PUTABLE IN THE 10TH AND</p>
<p>							   20 YEAR</p>
<p>((--U.S. Corporate Bond Unit, 212 859-167 ))</p>
</text>
